pable GPIO.\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\"source\": \"netlist\", \"quote\": \"(net (code \\\"144\\\") (name \\\"UART3_RX_FCC\\\") (class \\\"Default\\\") (node (ref \\\"FCC1\\\") (pin \\\"73\\\") (pinfunction \\\"VCAP\\\") (pintype \\\"power_out\\\"))\"},\n        {\"source\": \"netlist\", \"quote\": \"(node (ref \\\"FCC1\\\") (pin \\\"48\\\") (pinfunction \\\"VCAP\\\") (pintype \\\"power_out\\\"))\"}\n      ],\n      \"impact\": \"The core regulator output is shorted to the UART3 connector, which can disrupt the MCU core supply. UART3 is also not functional on any real MCU pin.\",\n      \"confidence\": 0.4\n    },\n    {\n      \"category\": \"open_connection\",\n      \"components\": [\"REG2\", \"FCC1\", \"NAVC1\"],\n      \"pins\": [\"REG2.1\", \"FCC1.27\", \"NAVC1.12\"],\n      \"nets\": [\"+3.3V\", \"+3V3\"],\n      \"observed\": \"The LDO output is on net '+3.3V', while the MCU and peripheral supply pins are on a separate net '+3V3'. The netlist shows no connection between them. The FCC1 VDD pins are on unconnected nets, and the NAVC1 VDD pins are also unconnected.\",\n      \"expected\": \"The 3.3 V LDO output should feed the MCU VDD pins and the sensor/pull-up 3V3 supply as one rail.\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\"source\": \"netlist\", \"quote\": \"(net (code \\\"1\\\") (name \\\"+3.3V\\\") (class \\\"Default\\\")\"},\n        {\"source\": \"netlist\", \"quote\": \"(net (code \\\"2\\\") (name \\\"+3V3\\\") (class \\\"Default\\\")\"},\n        {\"source\": \"spec\", \"quote\": \"3.3 V LDO (MCUs + sensors) | Hades (top sheet) | ST LD39200PU33R\"}\n      ],\n      \"impact\": \"If the two rails are not tied, the MCUs and their decoupling and pull-ups would be unpowered, so the boards would not run.\",\n      \"confidence\": 0.25\n    }\n  ],\n  \"summary\": \"The netlist shows the NAVC1 MCU's VSS pins isolated from GND, unlike the FCC1 MCU's VSS pins. Separately, the FCC1 VCAP pins are tied to the UART3 connector nets. The first finding is the 